searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"MedCore","doc":"Pure functional clinical signal and live-session domain core for MedEx.\n\nDefines stream contracts, live session state, preview vs. recording integrity\ntypes, product profile behaviours, and deterministic state-machine seams.","ref":"MedCore.html"},{"type":"function","title":"MedCore.version/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.html#version/0"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"MedCore.Profile","doc":"Behaviour implemented by clinical product applications to compose MedEx\ntransport archetypes, streams, inference hooks, and device control policies.","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Profile.inference_hook/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html#t:inference_hook/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Profile.topology/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html#t:topology/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"MedCore.Profile.control_policy/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html#c:control_policy/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"MedCore.Profile.inference_hooks/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html#c:inference_hooks/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"MedCore.Profile.streams/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html#c:streams/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"MedCore.Profile.topology/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html#c:topology/0"},{"type":"module","title":"MedCore.Session","doc":"Immutable live clinical transport session aggregate and pure reducer (`step/2`).\n\nA `Session` owns live participants, WebRTC connection attempts (`connection_id`),\ntransient preview interruptions, independent recording continuity, and device\nacquisitions (`acquisition_id`). It can outlast individual browser reconnects\nand supports standalone capture with `encounter_ref: nil` and no connected peer.","ref":"MedCore.Session.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.acquisition_id/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:acquisition_id/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.connection_id/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:connection_id/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.continuity_state/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:continuity_state/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.effect/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:effect/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.encounter_ref/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:encounter_ref/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.event/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:event/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.integrity_report/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:integrity_report/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.integrity_subject/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:integrity_subject/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.session_id/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:session_id/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.t/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedCore.Session.new/1","doc":"Constructs a new live clinical session. `encounter_ref` is optional (`nil` for standalone capture).","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#new/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedCore.Session.step/2","doc":"Pure state transition function `{next_session, effects} = step(session, event)`.","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#step/2"},{"type":"module","title":"MedCore.StreamSpec","doc":"Declarative contract for a clinical media, telemetry, or device control stream.","ref":"MedCore.StreamSpec.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.StreamSpec.archetype/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.StreamSpec.html#t:archetype/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.StreamSpec.integrity_policy/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.StreamSpec.html#t:integrity_policy/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.StreamSpec.t/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.StreamSpec.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"module","title":"MedRTC","doc":"OTP effect shell and WebRTC/Opus/SCTP runtime boundary for MedEx.\n\nOrchestrates live session coordination (`MedRTC.SessionServer`) and WebRTC\npeer negotiation (`MedRTC.PeerLoopback`) while delegating pure clinical signal\ninvariants to `MedCore.Session`.","ref":"MedRTC.html"},{"type":"module","title":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback","doc":"Minimal real `ExWebRTC.PeerConnection` SDP/ICE loopback harness used to\nexercise live WebRTC negotiation, peer disconnect, and replacement connection\nestablishment against `MedRTC.SessionServer`.","ref":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.negotiated_pair/0","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.html#t:negotiated_pair/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.close_pair/1","doc":"Closes both `ExWebRTC.PeerConnection` processes in a negotiated pair.","ref":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.html#close_pair/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.connect_pair/2","doc":"Starts two real `ExWebRTC.PeerConnection` instances with an `:audio`\ntransceiver, exchanges SDP offer/answer and ICE candidates, and waits until\nboth peers reach `:connected`.","ref":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.html#connect_pair/2"},{"type":"module","title":"MedRTC.Preview","doc":"One replaceable, send-only WebRTC peer for an Opus preview. The caller owns\nthe peer and receives its ExWebRTC state changes. Capture has its own lifetime.","ref":"MedRTC.Preview.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedRTC.Preview.t/0","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.Preview.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.Preview.answer/1","doc":"Answers a receive-only audio offer containing the browser's ICE candidates.","ref":"MedRTC.Preview.html#answer/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.Preview.close/1","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.Preview.html#close/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.Preview.send_opus/3","doc":"Sends one 20 ms Opus frame. Frame indices are relative to the acquisition.","ref":"MedRTC.Preview.html#send_opus/3"},{"type":"module","title":"MedRTC.SessionServer","doc":"OTP `GenServer` owning a live `%MedCore.Session{}` and dispatching emitted\nproducer facts to registered subscribers.","ref":"MedRTC.SessionServer.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedRTC.SessionServer.start_opt/0","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.SessionServer.html#t:start_opt/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.SessionServer.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"MedRTC.SessionServer.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.SessionServer.dispatch/2","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.SessionServer.html#dispatch/2"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.SessionServer.snapshot/1","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.SessionServer.html#snapshot/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.SessionServer.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.SessionServer.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"MedRTC.WavCapture","doc":"Pure-Elixir 16-bit PCM WAV parser and one-input / two-output clinical capture\nrunner.\n\nStreams chunks from a real WAV recording (such as a PhysioNet CirCor\nDigiScope phonocardiogram) to two independent outputs:\n\n1. An optional live preview callback (which may drop or reconnect with a\n   browser/WebRTC peer mid-capture).\n2. An independent lossless PCM collector that computes the exact decoded\n   sample count, duration, SHA-256 digest, and continuity state\n   (`:observed_continuous | :observed_gap | :unknown`) for `MedCore.Session`.","ref":"MedRTC.WavCapture.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedRTC.WavCapture.capture_summary/0","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.WavCapture.html#t:capture_summary/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedRTC.WavCapture.parsed_wav/0","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.WavCapture.html#t:parsed_wav/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.WavCapture.encode_pcm16_wav/2","doc":"Encodes raw 16-bit signed little-endian mono PCM into a standard RIFF/WAVE\nbinary.","ref":"MedRTC.WavCapture.html#encode_pcm16_wav/2"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.WavCapture.parse_wav/1","doc":"Parses an uncompressed PCM WAV binary (handling arbitrary RIFF chunks before\n`fmt ` and `data`, as emitted by clinical recorders and PhysioNet CirCor).","ref":"MedRTC.WavCapture.html#parse_wav/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.WavCapture.record/4","doc":"Paces a verified WAV fixture and atomically finalizes its original PCM in\na playable WAV. The paired Ogg file contains 20 ms Opus frames derived from\nthe same input. Preview is best-effort and can stall or fail independently.\n\nRun this operation in the acquisition task. Supply `:on_preview_frame`\nto receive `(frame_index, opus_payload)` from the preview worker.","ref":"MedRTC.WavCapture.html#record/4"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.WavCapture.replay/2","doc":"Replays a parsed WAV through one input into two independent outputs:\na live preview sink (`:on_preview_chunk`) and a lossless capture collector.\n\nOptions:\n- `:acquisition_id` (required)\n- `:started_at_ms` (default `0`)\n- `:chunk_ms` (default `20`)\n- `:on_preview_chunk` (`fn chunk_idx, pcm_chunk -> :ok | {:error, term()} end`, optional)\n- `:drop_capture_indices` (`MapSet` or list of chunk indices simulating real capture loss)\n- `:continuity_observable?` (default `true`; when `false`, reports `:unknown`)","ref":"MedRTC.WavCapture.html#replay/2"},{"type":"module","title":"MedWeb","doc":"Reusable Phoenix signaling contract (`MedWeb.Signaling`) and shipped browser\n`RTCPeerConnection` hook assets for MedEx live sessions.","ref":"MedWeb.html"},{"type":"module","title":"MedWeb.Signaling","doc":"Browser signaling message normalization and reconnect handshake contract for\nMedEx live sessions.","ref":"MedWeb.Signaling.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedWeb.Signaling.client_signal/0","doc":"","ref":"MedWeb.Signaling.html#t:client_signal/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedWeb.Signaling.hook_asset_full_path/0","doc":"Resolves the absolute path to the shipped browser hook asset whether loaded\nfrom `:med_web` in source mode or from the Welded `:med_ex` SDK package.","ref":"MedWeb.Signaling.html#hook_asset_full_path/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedWeb.Signaling.hook_asset_path/0","doc":"Returns the shipped browser hook asset relative path inside `priv/`.","ref":"MedWeb.Signaling.html#hook_asset_path/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedWeb.Signaling.to_session_event/1","doc":"Normalizes a browser signaling event into a pure `MedCore.Session` event.","ref":"MedWeb.Signaling.html#to_session_event/1"},{"type":"extras","title":"Overview","doc":"# MedEx\n\n`MedEx` is a reusable Elixir SDK poncho for live clinical device sessions, WebRTC transport, and independent recording integrity. It separates what the clinician hears live over WebRTC from what the device records losslessly, so a browser disconnect never corrupts or mislabels a clinical capture.\n\nThe repository is a non-umbrella Elixir poncho managed with Blitz (parallel checks) and Weld (single-artifact SDK projection). Downstream apps such as `med_fabric/apps/exam` consume one OTP application (`:med_ex`), never individual internal path dependencies.\n\n---","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"What This Owns (and Does Not Own) - Overview","doc":"**`med_ex` owns:**\n- Pure live-session state transitions (`MedCore.Session`) with a four-level identity model (`encounter_ref`, `session_id`, `connection_id`, `acquisition_id`) and separate integrity tracking for `{:preview_stream, stream_id}` vs. `{:recording_artifact, acquisition_id}`.\n- OTP runtime and WebRTC/audio transport (`MedRTC.SessionServer`, `MedRTC.PeerLoopback` over `ExWebRTC`, `MedRTC.WavCapture` one-input/two-output WAV replay).\n- Reusable signaling event helpers and the shipped browser WebRTC JavaScript hook (`MedWeb.Signaling`, `priv/static/med_web/session_hook.js`).\n- Opt-in real-time signal/inference contracts (`MedAdapters.Inference`, excluded from the default `:med_ex` projection).\n- A minimal standalone reference app (`apps/med_pulse`) proving `:med_ex` works without `encounter_ref` or `med_fabric`.\n\n**`med_ex` does not own:**\n- Durable clinical encounters, clinician observation acceptance, transactional outbox storage, HL7 FHIR delivery, or production Phoenix endpoints/LiveViews/signaling channels. Those live in the companion `med_fabric` workspace (`med_fabric/apps/exam` consumes `:med_ex` one-way).\n\n---","ref":"readme.html#what-this-owns-and-does-not-own"},{"type":"extras","title":"Package Map - Overview","doc":"| Package | Path | Included in `:med_ex` SDK? | Implemented Today | Documentation |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **MedCore** | `core/med_core` | Yes | `MedCore.Session`, `MedCore.StreamSpec`, `MedCore.Profile` | [core/med_core/README.md](core/med_core/README.md) |\n| **MedRTC** | `core/med_rtc` | Yes | `MedRTC.SessionServer`, `MedRTC.PeerLoopback` (`ExWebRTC`), `MedRTC.WavCapture` | [core/med_rtc/README.md](core/med_rtc/README.md) |\n| **MedWeb** | `core/med_web` | Yes | `MedWeb.Signaling`, `priv/static/med_web/session_hook.js` | [core/med_web/README.md](core/med_web/README.md) |\n| **MedAdapters** | `core/med_adapters` | No (opt-in source) | `MedAdapters.Inference` behaviour + advisory envelope | [core/med_adapters/README.md](core/med_adapters/README.md) |\n| **MedPulse** | `apps/med_pulse` | No (proof app) | `MedPulse.ClinicalProfile` + standalone WAV/reconnect test | [apps/med_pulse/README.md](apps/med_pulse/README.md) |\n\n---","ref":"readme.html#package-map"},{"type":"extras","title":"Walkthrough: Reconnect & Independent Capture Integrity - Overview","doc":"Trace this path in `core/med_rtc/test/wav_capture_test.exs` and `core/med_core/test/med_core_test.exs`:\n\n1. Start a `MedCore.Session` inside `MedRTC.SessionServer` and connect a real `ExWebRTC` loopback peer (`conn_a`).\n2. Start an acquisition (`acq_1`) and replay a 4 kHz 16-bit mono PCM WAV (such as PhysioNet CirCor DigiScope `2530_AV.wav`) through `MedRTC.WavCapture.replay/2`.\n3. Drop the live WebRTC preview (`conn_a`) mid-capture so 40 preview chunks fail while the lossless collector records all 94,400 samples with an unchanged SHA-256 digest.\n4. Dispatch `capture_completed` (and dispatch it a second time with a new `delivery_id`), then reconnect the clinician on `conn_b`.\n5. `MedCore.Session` records one closed preview interruption on `{:preview_stream, \"auscultation\"}`, marks `{:recording_artifact, \"acq_1\"}` as `:observed_continuous`, ignores late disconnects from replaced `conn_a`, deduplicates identical completion deliveries, and flags conflicting digests as `:conflict`.\n\n---","ref":"readme.html#walkthrough-reconnect-independent-capture-integrity"},{"type":"extras","title":"Commands & Verification - Overview","doc":"Toolchain pins live in `.tool-versions` (`erlang 29.1.2`, `elixir 1.20.5-otp-29`). Ordinary Elixir, Blitz, and Weld checks run without external services once dependencies are installed.\n\n```bash\n# Inner dev loop (parallel across all 5 child projects via Blitz)\nmix deps.get\nmix monorepo.deps.get\nmix ci\nmix monorepo.dialyzer\nmix monorepo.docs && mix docs\n\n# Welded :med_ex SDK projection & provenance checks\nmix med_ex.projection.refresh\nmix med_ex.projection.status --strict\nmix weld.inspect\nmix weld.verify\n\n# Publish verified projection to orphan branch projection/med_ex\nmix weld.release.prepare\nmix weld.release.track --push\n\n# Optional: download real PhysioNet CirCor 2530_AV.wav (gitignored) & verify PCM SHA-256 via uv\n./fixtures/circor/prepare.sh\nUV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=\"$HOME/.cache/med_ex/waveforms-venv\" \\\n  uv run --locked --project tools/waveforms \\\n  python tools/waveforms/check_wav.py fixtures/circor/2530_AV.wav\n```\n\n> **Note on `UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT`**: Keeping the Python venv under `~/.cache/med_ex/waveforms-venv` avoids placing external interpreter symlinks inside the Git working tree, keeping `mix_workspace_ops doctor` clean.\n\n> **Current verification boundary**: ExWebRTC peer negotiation, WAV replay across preview drops, JS hook syntax (`node --check`), and Weld packaging are verified automatically in CI. A live desktop-browser audio run (MedEx server → real Chromium/Firefox browser via `session_hook.js`) remains an open desktop-browser exit criterion because this headless host has no Chromium/Playwright installed.\n\n---","ref":"readme.html#commands-verification"},{"type":"extras","title":"Upstream Ecosystem - Overview","doc":"- Blitz: https://github.com/nshkrdotcom/blitz\n- Weld: https://github.com/nshkrdotcom/weld\n- ExWebRTC: https://github.com/elixir-webrtc/ex_webrtc\n- LiveExWebRTC: https://github.com/elixir-webrtc/live_ex_webrtc\n- ExSCTP: https://github.com/elixir-webrtc/ex_sctp\n- Membrane Core: https://github.com/membraneframework/membrane_core\n- PhysioNet CirCor DigiScope Phonocardiogram Dataset: https://physionet.org/content/circor-heart-sound/1.0.3/","ref":"readme.html#upstream-ecosystem"},{"type":"extras","title":"License - Overview","doc":"MIT — see [LICENSE](LICENSE).","ref":"readme.html#license"},{"type":"extras","title":"Browser capture architecture - Overview","doc":"```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    WAV[\"Verified PCM WAV\"] --> Capture[\"Paced capture task\"]\n    Capture --> Artifact[\"Finalized WAV + PCM digest\"]\n    Opus[\"Opus preview from the same fixture\"] --> Preview[\"Bounded preview worker\"]\n    Capture -->|\"20 ms frame index\"| Preview\n    Preview --> Peer[\"Replaceable ExWebRTC peer\"]\n    Peer --> Browser[\"Clinician audio track\"]\n    Browser <-->|\"SDP with gathered ICE\"| Host[\"Authorized host signaling channel\"]\n    Host --> Peer\n    Artifact --> Host\n```\n\nThe host starts `MedRTC.WavCapture.record/4` in an acquisition task. A separate worker supplies best-effort Opus preview frames. The browser's peer can close or rejoin without interrupting the acquisition. The task returns a finalized WAV path, decoded PCM SHA-256, retained frame count, duration and measured continuity. The host owns access to the artifact and starts any review or clinical persistence.\n\nTo prepare the real fixture with the shipped lock, install curl and uv and run `./fixtures/circor/prepare.sh /path/to/cache` from the source checkout. For a Welded SDK, run `bash  /priv/fixtures/prepare.sh /path/to/cache`. uv resolves Python 3.12.14 and the pinned FFmpeg wheel for the host. The script verifies the original WAV before producing its 20 ms Opus preview. The fixture is distributed separately from the SDK and retains the attribution recorded in `priv/fixtures/MANIFEST.json`.\n\nThe reusable browser hook is created by `createMedExHook(Socket)` from the packaged `priv/static/med_web/session_hook.js`. The host supplies its Phoenix Socket constructor, a signed token in the hook element, and an encounter topic. The preview owns the browser connection. The host authorizes it and hands the gathered offer to `MedRTC.Preview.answer/1`.","ref":"readme.html#browser-capture-architecture"},{"type":"extras","title":"Changelog","doc":"# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to the `med_ex` poncho workspace will be documented in this file.\n\n## [0.1.0] - 2026-11-22","ref":"changelog.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Added - Changelog","doc":"- Initialized the `med_ex` non-umbrella Elixir poncho workspace with Blitz and Weld orchestration.\n- Added architecture documentation and skeleton packages under `core/` (`med_core`, `med_rtc`, `med_adapters`, `med_web`) and `apps/` (`med_pulse`).\n- Configured Credo, Dialyxir, ExDoc, custom SVG branding assets, and per-package metadata across every child Mix project.","ref":"changelog.html#added"},{"type":"extras","title":"License","doc":"MIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 nshkrdotcom\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.","ref":"license.html"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.40.5"}}